														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2691725">
									

<p>Gamers Against Weed is the first 21st-century GOI (shut up Anderson Robotics, nobody likes you). Most SCPs float off in some sort of timeless void where they work equally well in 2016 as they do in 1996 and 1976, except when they mention computers or the internet, but even then the internet is often just a vector for the SCP in question or a throwaway line in the containment procedures.</p>
<p>You can make most of the other GOIs work in the present day, but if they're part of a larger social context at all they're distinctly 20th-century, if not older. Gamers Against Weed's inclusion says that a story takes place HERE and NOW, and it's about relationships and trends and movements with which the reader can relate to at best and identify at worst.</p>
<p>By comparison, Are We Cool Yet is what a bunch of gamers and students think dada is and/or when they want to be meta. Not that good things can't come of it, but its inclusion in an article sets an entirely different tone than Gamers Against Weed.</p>

