<p>There are a lot of things to like here.</p>
<ul>
<li>&quot;+1 for anomalous pranks and tricks&quot; is a good way to sum up my feelings about this &#8212; a dumb online inside joke getting waaay out of hand is a great premise for an SCP.</li>
<li>It memorably renders chatroom banter &#8212; everything from the usernames to the jokes to the cadence is larger than life in a good way.</li>
<li>The eponymous inside joke is, itself, incredibly funny for no reason I can adequately explain.</li>
<li>Lastly, I really like this take on Gamers Against Weed &#8212; while my 2842 sorta set the tone for them, 2293 does the heavy lifting of their actual characterization: sorta out-of-control, but very much human; disruptive, but with a good heart and a love of fun; extremely online, but not gratingly so. It's everything I had hoped for.</li>
</ul>

